notes="# Eirene MOS 3.1.0 UART0 RC1\n\nThis candidate lets an aware app calculate while MOS sends its borrowed buffer\nto the VDP using UART interrupts and16-byte OTIRX refills. Ordinary startup and\nRST18 stay upstream Eirene paths. It is an opt-in extension in bgates747's fork,\nnot an upstream Eirene release or a stable/default MOS recommendation.\n\nSource commit: @COMMIT@\nUpstream base/tag:86b694260e3be3b391284ce4aa8ecc758f7f34e9 /3.1.0_beta_1.\nProposed candidate tag:3.1.0_uart0_rc_1, on codex/uart0-async; main is unchanged.\nMOS image:@BYTES@bytes, CRC32@CRC@; SHA256@SHA@.\nExact-image hardware qualification: PENDING. This prepared package is not yet\npublished. Model checks passed; prior physical measurements below concern the\npre-branding image. The final published prerelease must replace this pending\nstatement with its exact-image hardware evidence.\n\n## Files and building\n\nmos-rc1.bin/map: exact candidate and linker map. source/: full matching MOS tree,\nincluding licenses, reference and caller documentation. fixture/: matching\nno-argument regression app source. example/: small original C app and thin ABI\nbridge. test.bin, example.bin and checks.bin: ready applications/comparator.\nBuild-info.json records compiler/binutils/library hashes, commit and generated\napp identities. evidence/: model results and pre-branding physical results.\nSHA256SUMS covers every file except itself. The custom diagnostic VDP is not\nincluded in this MOS release ZIP; firmware under test uses ordinary VDP commands.\n\nOn Oryx, use AgonDev, retaining the toolchain identities in build-info.json:\n\n```\nmake -C source AGONDEV_TOOLCHAIN=/absolute/path/to/agondev\nmake -C fixture AGONDEV_TOOLCHAIN=/absolute/path/to/agondev\nmake -C example AGONDEV_TOOLCHAIN=/absolute/path/to/agondev\n```\n\nThe generated identity headers in the app sources match the included MOS bytes.\nNo ZDS II tool or HEX converter is used for this Eirene build. Source checkout\nalso includes experiments/uart0-release/prepare.py for two-build reproduction.\nRetain matching Agon libraries; hashes identify the exact qualification tools.\n\n## Install and test\n\nCopy this directory to /test/mos-uart0 on the Agon's SD. Keep the known official\nstock restoration mos-stock.bin available. Use the normal installed MOSlet:\n`flash mos mos-rc1.bin`. Keep its ordinary updater checks and reboot as prompted.\nConfirm the Eirene UART0 MOS Version3.1.0 RC1 banner (spaces may separate RC/1).\nCold boot once. Return to /test/mos-uart0; type `test`, wait for RC1 PASS and the\nnormal prompt, then type `test` again. Finally type `example` and require\nRC1 EXAMPLE PASS. No arguments, LOAD or RUN. Allow two minutes per test; a stall\nis failure. Reports use sequential Rnnnn.log and next.txt, with runs.log tracking\nSTART/PASS. Keep failed reports too. This tests ordinary output before and after\nopt-in, callback/NULL callback, single-source/BUSY, boundaries, concurrent RX,\nsource reuse, explicit finish, all8192received payload bytes and normal return.\nThe simple example prints its result; it does not create a benchmark report.\n\nNo VDP protocol modification is introduced by the sender. Receiver regression\nand performance qualification used VDP2.16.0 with the separate receive-recovery\nfix; see the source task records. This ZIP does not assert equivalent stress\nqualification on stock VDP. Use the project's staged matched VDP for the RC\nqualification run. Do not change VDP merely to use the syscall in an app.\n\nFor ordinary restoration, use `flash mos mos-stock.bin` and reboot normally.\nIf MOS cannot boot, use AgonPlatform/agon-recovery with the board's documented\nZDI wiring; do not substitute unverified pin diagrams. Stock restoration image:\nofficial MOS3.0.2, SHA256d564243283972690933a4554296ad6202ca4ef54572279533a942960846bebae.\nThe normal CLI firmware updater and recovery procedure remain unmodified.\n\n## Application contract and scope\n\nRead source/docs/uart0-async.md and source/docs/tasks/TM-001/contract.md.\nFork-local syscalls42h=submit and43h=finish; ADL1/MBASE0, EI, foreground only.\nOne immutable source outstanding, no queue or implicit app-exit cleanup.\nArm state before submit. The bounded DI callback only posts state; source\nrelease is not wire drain or receiver completion. Finish before normal output,\nreturning, freeing code/data or handing UART ownership to anything else.\nThe example guards its ROM identity before making these fork-specific calls.\n\nConsole8 pre-branding measurements found64.06% more paced foreground calculation\nthan stock; flat-out sending retained85.5% of no-traffic calculation rate at\nessentially stock throughput. Those are controlled calculation measurements,\nnot exclusive CPU-utilization figures, indefinite-rate or real-app claims.\nOther boards, EMOS size/compatibility and real audio deadlines remain unqualified.\n\nBased on Tom Morton's Eirene and supplied async_vdu.asm; retain the full original\nsources and attributions. MOS copyright includes Dean Belfield and the upstream\nAgon contributors. Original notices, FatFS/ChaN and allocator/library notices\nremain in source/ and licenses/. Our additions retain the project's MIT terms;\nno third-party notice is replaced. This candidate is independent of upstream\nacceptance by Tom or the AgonPlatform maintainers.\n"
